pve-storage-quantastor (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v1.0.0 — first general-availability release of the QuantaStor storage
    plugin for Proxmox VE (VM disks and LXC containers on iSCSI block
    volumes). Changes since 0.2.1:
  * Containers: rootdir content type (block-based rootdir, same model as
    RBD/LVM-thin); filesystem-consistent snapshots of running containers via
    volume_snapshot_needs_fsfreeze; restart migration; extra mount points;
    pct fstrim discard passthrough; unprivileged containers. CT templates
    (vztmpl) deliberately unsupported — keep them on a file-based storage.
  * Thin provisioning: volume_create now sends thinProvisioned explicitly
    (absent boolean meant thick — every volume was 100% space-reserved); the
    previously-dead 'sparse' storage.cfg option is honored, default ON.
  * UI: Content selector offers Disk image + Container as a multi-select
    (was single-select); both preselected on the Add dialog.
  * free_image: falls back to per-snapshot deletion when a cascade delete
    fails or partially completes; retries the volume delete through brief
    post-teardown busy windows.
  * Session waits now default to 200s (was 30s; create_base previously passed
    an explicit 120s) so snapshot rollback and template conversion outlast
    QuantaStor's session-manager refresh cycle, which has a hardcoded 180s
    floor and cannot be tuned lower. Shorter waits failed deterministically
    when issued soon after a stop, and the failed PVE task left a rollback
    lock that blocked every subsequent start.
  * activate_volume: retries the ACL add through transient 5xx responses.
    QuantaStor serves a clone as an async ZFS "instant replica" and can return
    the volume before SCST has created its iSCSI target, so the ACL add came
    back "HTTP 500 interrupted by signal" and killed roughly half of clones.
    The add is idempotent, so retrying is safe; non-5xx failures (auth,
    not-found) still fail immediately instead of stalling for the budget.
  * README: container usage + limitations, err=493 troubleshooting incl. the
    server-side fix, content-type/pre-start gotcha.
  * Recommended appliance build: a current QuantaStor 7 build carrying the
    server-side fix for the template-conversion rename wedge and the
    fresh-snapshot delete window.

 -- OSNexus <support@osnexus.com>  Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:09:46 +0000

pve-storage-quantastor (0.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * APIClient: send HTTP Basic credentials preemptively instead of via LWP
    challenge-response ($ua->credentials). QuantaStor REST endpoints often do
    not issue a 401 WWW-Authenticate Basic challenge (and the realm varies
    across versions), so the old client attached no Authorization header and
    the appliance returned "[err=26] Authentication check failed" even when the
    password was correct (curl -u works because it sends Basic preemptively).
    Removes all dependence on the challenge and realm.
  * Adds regression tests asserting the real UserAgent carries a single-line
    Authorization: Basic header.
  * README: err=26 troubleshooting now leads with this cause and curl
    reproduction commands; docs use release-version terms.

 -- OSNexus <support@osnexus.com>  Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:15:55 +0000

pve-storage-quantastor (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v0.2.0 — first-class PVE storage type 'quantastor' (no PVE core patching).
  * PVE::Storage::QuantaStor::APIClient: OO REST client for the QuantaStor API.
  * PVE::Storage::QuantaStor::ISCSIManager: iSCSI initiator lifecycle
    management (login/logout/discovery/rescan).
  * PVE::Storage::Custom::QuantaStor: full storage plugin covering all hooks —
    activate, status, list, alloc, free, path, online resize (flags=2),
    snapshot, rollback, clone, and template creation.
  * PVE::API2::Storage::QuantaStorScan: pool-scan API endpoint
    (GET /nodes/<node>/scan/quantastor), injected into Scan.pm by postinst.
  * Web UI dialog: storage-ID auto-fill (qs-storage-N), pool scan dropdown,
    content type locked to 'Disk image'.
  * Password stored in /etc/pve/priv/storage/<id>.pw (pmxcfs-replicated),
    never written to storage.cfg.
  * dpkg file triggers re-inject the UI script tag and scan endpoint after
    pve-manager / pve-storage upgrades.
  * Validated on PVE 9.1.x and 9.2.x, including two-node cluster live
    migration. Loads on both (api=13).

 -- OSNexus <support@osnexus.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 21:59:09 +0000
